UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Data is reshaping every field—from healthcare, sports, and business to social sciences, engineering, and the environment. The Bachelor of Applied Data Science (BADS) is designed for students from diverse backgrounds to help them enhance their primary discipline with in-demand data science skills. Regardless of your field of study, this program… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-18nu28r-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Data is reshaping every field—from healthcare, sports, and business to social sciences, engineering, and the environment. The Bachelor of Applied Data Science (BADS) is designed for students from diverse backgrounds to help them enhance their primary discipline with in-demand data science skills. Regardless of your field of study, this program will empower you to extract insights, solve complex problems, and make data-driven decisions in your area of expertise.</p> <p>The BADS curriculum provides a strong foundation in <strong>data wrangling and visualisation, database management, programming, and statistical fundamentals</strong>, ensuring accessibility for students without prior computing experience. Through directed courses such as <strong>predictive analytics, applied artificial intelligence, big data, data mining, cloud computing, optimisation, and business intelligence, </strong>students can tailor their learning to complement their core discipline.</p> <p>With a focus on applied problem-solving and industry relevance, this program equips graduates to integrate data science into their field, unlocking new opportunities and career paths. No matter your background, this degree provides the tools to thrive in an increasingly data-driven world.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '1 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>This program is only available to current University of Newcastle students who are wishing to study concurrently, in addition to their primary program.</p> <p>Admission to this program is available to Australian citizens and residents only.</p> <p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p>To be eligible for admission, a student must attain a minimum ATAR of 65, or the equivalent rank for their primary undergraduate degree.</p> <p>Students who are enrolled in any of the below programs, will be excluded from enrolling into the B Applied Data Science programs due to substantial course overlap:</p> <ul> <li>Bachelor of Information Technology</li> <li>Bachelor of Computer Science</li> <li>Bachelor of Mathematics</li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Applied Data Science is not a stand-alone program. It is designed to be completed as a bolt-on program, alongside an undergraduate program (primary program). </p> <p>The volume of learning for this program is 240 units.</p> <p>Students must complete 80 units of unique courses as part of the B Applied Data Science program. The remaining 160 units will be made up of the requirements of your primary program. </p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50095?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">A Bachelor of Arts degree enables you to study what you are passionate about in life, and to gather skills that will prepare for the work place and a wide variety of careers. You have the flexibility to choose from a broad range of majors and minors, taught face to… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-8h97uo-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>A Bachelor of Arts degree enables you to study what you are passionate about in life, and to gather skills that will prepare for the work place and a wide variety of careers. You have the flexibility to choose from a broad range of majors and minors, taught face to face, online, and on different campuses. You will take 30 units of Core courses across the BA degree, enabling you to become part of a common group in your first year and to focus on specific knowledge and skills you need to obtain for success. You can tailor the remainder of your program to match your specific interests, including pursuing themes and disciplines, gaining work experience, engaging with industry, and completing research projects.</p> <p>Some majors/minors are offered predominantly at one campus and others are offered at both the Callaghan and Ourimbah campus or online. The availability of courses within the below listed majors/minors are subject to change.</p> <p>The offerings in the Bachelor of Arts are diverse. Students must complete at least one major, with options to complement this with a second major, pair of minors or a range of electives. The Program requirements are detailed below.</p> <p><strong>Majors and Minors:</strong></p> <ul><li>English &amp; Writing</li><li>Screen and Cultural Studies</li><li>French Studies (either Beginner or Intermediate Sequence)</li><li>Global Indigenous Studies</li><li>History</li><li>Human Geography &amp; the Environment</li><li>International Relations</li><li>Japanese Studies (either Beginner or Intermediate Sequence)</li><li>Linguistics</li><li>Performing Arts</li><li>Psychology Studies</li><li>Sociology &amp; Anthropology</li></ul> <p><strong>Minors only:</strong></p> <ul><li>Ancient History</li><li>Chinese</li><li>Education</li><li>Gender and Sexuality Studies</li><li>Information Technology</li><li>Studies of Philosophy, Religion and Ethics </li><li>Violence Studies</li><li>Writing Studies</li></ul> <p><em>All majors and minors are available at Callaghan campus, with the exception of Performing Arts and International Relations and Screen and Cultural Studies which are available at Newcastle City campus. </em> </p> <p><em>The majors and minors available Online are: English and Writing, Screen and Cultural Studies, French Studies, Global Indigenous Studies, History, Japanese Studies, Psychology Studies, and Sociology and Anthropology.</em> </p> <p><em>The availability of courses within majors and minors are subject to change.</em> </p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '3 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Arts requires students to successfully complete 240 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>30 units of core courses;</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement course list;</li><li>one 80 unit Arts major; and</li><li>120 units of electives. Refer to the pathway information below*</li></ul> <p>Students must complete a minimum of 40 units at each level (1000, 2000, 3000). </p> <p>Students must not exceed 100 units at 1000 level. </p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 240 units.</p> <p><strong>*Pathway Information</strong></p> <p>Students must complete at least one Arts major sequence to fulfil the requirements of their program.</p> <p>Students may utilise their elective courses to undertake a major pathway, detailed below. Students must ensure that each major has 60 units of unique courses.</p> <ol><li>Single Major pathway A - one 80 unit major, one 40 unit minor and 80 units of electives</li><li>Single Major pathway B - one 80 unit major, two 40 unit minors and 40 units of electives</li><li>Single Major pathway C - one 80 unit major and 120 units of electives</li><li>Double Major pathway A - two 80 unit majors and one 40 unit minor</li><li>Double Major pathway B - two 80 unit majors, no minor and 40 units of electives</li></ol> <p><strong>Major</strong></p> <p>A major must comprise of 80 units of compulsory courses and or courses from the Course List from one area as follows:</p> <ul><li>A minimum of 10 units at 1000 level. French Studies (Intermediate Sequence) Japanese Studies (Intermediate Sequence) and International Relations are excluded from this rule.</li><li>A minimum of 40 units at 3000 level</li></ul> <p><strong>Minor</strong></p> <p>A minor must comprise of 40 units of compulsory courses and or courses from the Course List from one area as follows:</p> <ul><li>A minimum of 10 units at 1000 level. International Relations is excluded from this rule. </li><li>At least 20 units at 2000 or 3000 level</li></ul> <p>All students, please note:</p> <ol><li>Each course can only be counted once towards a major/minor or elective</li><li>When you have successfully completed your program, your transcript will specify completed major/s but will not specify completed minors</li><li>Full-time enrolment (80 units per year) will enable program completion in 3 yrs. Students may enrol in less per year but completion will take proportionately longer.</li></ol> <p><strong>Psychology Studies Major/Minor</strong></p> <p>The Psychology major/minor is for students with a general interest in Psychology. Since 2012 it has not been accredited by the Australian Psychology Accreditation Council (APAC).</p> <p><strong>Languages</strong></p> <p>Students who already possess knowledge of the French or Japanese languages (eg HSC Continuers or equivalent) are advised to consult with the French or Japanese Studies Discipline Convenor BEFORE enrolling into the French or Japanese Studies (Intermediate Sequence).</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '001602K';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Students who perform well during their Bachelor of Arts or equivalent program, with a GPA of 5.0 or greater, may apply to undertake a further year of full-time (or part-time equivalent) study to obtain an Bachelor of Arts (Honours) degree. The Honours program allows students to further develop their specific… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-a00ao3-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Students who perform well during their Bachelor of Arts or equivalent program, with a GPA of 5.0 or greater, may apply to undertake a further year of full-time (or part-time equivalent) study to obtain an Bachelor of Arts (Honours) degree. The Honours program allows students to further develop their specific areas of interest.</p> <p>Students undertake the Honours program from one of the following discipline areas:</p> <ul><li>Ancient History</li><li>Chinese</li><li>Creative and Performing Arts</li><li>English and Writing</li><li>French Studies</li><li>German</li><li>Global Indigenous Studies</li><li>History</li><li>International Relations</li><li>Japanese</li><li>Linguistics</li><li>Philosophy</li><li>Screen and Cultural Studies</li><li>Sociology and Anthropology</li></ul></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '1 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants having completed a Bachelor degree in a cognate area with a minimum GPA of 5.0:</p> <ul> <li>across all studies undertaken within the program; or</li> <li>across a major in the proposed area of study; or</li> <li>across 80 units of 3000 level courses (which must include at least 40 units of 3000 level courses in the major where a major exists); or</li> <li>where the applicant has completed less than 80 units at 3000 level, a GPA of 5.0 calculated from at least 60 units of 3000 level courses (which includes at least 40 units of 3000 level courses in the major where a major exists).</li> </ul> <p>In exceptional circumstances, an application which does not meet the above requirements may be considered.</p> <p>Domestic applicants should apply using the direct <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/apply/end_on_honours">End-On Honours online application form</a>.</p> <p>International applicants should apply using the direct International <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions">application portal</a>. For more information see <a href="https://askuon-future.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/419/kw/international%20applicant">How do I apply as an International Student?</a></p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>This program requires the successful completion of 80 units of core courses. </p> <p>Students undertake the Honours program from one of the following discipline areas:</p> <ul><li>Ancient History</li><li>Chinese</li><li>Creative and Performing Arts</li><li>English and Writing</li><li>French Studies</li><li>German</li><li>Global Indigenous Studies</li><li>History</li><li>International Relations</li><li>Japanese</li><li>Linguistics</li><li>Philosophy</li><li>Screen and Cultural Studies</li><li>Sociology and Anthropology</li></ul> <p>Students who wish to complete the Honours program in two discipline areas should apply to the Program Convenor.</p> <p>Course supervisory arrangements will be flexible across campus locations and/or zoom where appropriate</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40209?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Arts/Bachelor of Innovation and Entrepreneurship (BArts/BIE) is a 320 unit Bachelor degree. Students must complete 190 units of core courses and the compulsory courses and/or courses chosen from a course list from one major. The program is designed to provide students who wish to combine their knowledge,… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-53aban-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Arts/Bachelor of Innovation and Entrepreneurship (BArts/BIE) is a 320 unit Bachelor degree. Students must complete 190 units of core courses and the compulsory courses and/or courses chosen from a course list from one major. The program is designed to provide students who wish to combine their knowledge, strengths and interests in arts, culture, heritage and humanities with innovative business and entrepreneurial skills in an original program of study.</p> <p>You can choose a major and minor in the following areas (subject to change):</p> <ul><li>Ancient History (Minor only)</li><li>Chinese (Minor only)</li><li>Creative &amp; Performing Arts</li><li>Education</li><li>English &amp; Writing</li><li>French Studies (Beginner Sequence)</li><li>French Studies (Intermediate Sequence)</li><li>Gender and Sexuality Studies (Minor only)</li><li>German</li><li>Global Indigenous Studies</li><li>History</li><li>Human Geography &amp; the Environment</li><li>Information Technology (Minor only)</li><li>Japanese Studies (Beginner Sequence)</li><li>Japanese Studies (Intermediate Sequence)</li><li>Linguistics</li><li>Politics &amp; International Relations</li><li>Psychology Studies</li><li>Screen and Cultural Studies</li><li>Sociology &amp; Anthropology</li><li>Studies of Religion (Minor only)</li><li>Violence Studies (Minor only)</li><li>Writing Studies (Minor only)</li></ul></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum selection rank, or satisfying the requirements for an approved admission scheme.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Arts/Bachelor of Innovation and Entrepreneurship requires to successfully complete 320 units, which is comprised of: </p> <ul><li>160 units of Innovation and Entrepreneurship core courses; </li><li>30 units of Arts core courses; </li><li>One 80 unit Arts major;</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement course list; and</li><li>40 units of electives<strong> OR</strong> a 40 unit Arts minor. </li></ul> <p>Students must not exceed a maximum of 100 units at any level in each of the component programs.</p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 320 units. </p> <p><strong>Major</strong></p> <p>A major must comprise of 80 units from one area as follows:· </p> <ul><li>A minimum of 10 units at 1000 level. French Studies (Intermediate Sequence) and Japanese Studies (Intermediate Sequence) are excluded from this rule.</li><li>A minimum of 40 units at 3000 level</li></ul> <p><strong>Minor</strong></p> <p>A minor must comprise of 40 units of compulsory and or courses chosen from a course list from one area as follows:</p> <ul><li>A minimum of 10 units at 1000 level </li><li>At least 20 units at 2000 or 3000 level</li></ul> <p>All students, please note:</p> <ol><li>Each course can only be counted once towards a major/minor or elective</li><li>When you have successfully completed your program, your transcript will specify completed major/s but will not specify completed minors</li><li>Full-time enrolment (80 units per year) will enable program completion in 4 yrs. Students may enrol in less per year but completion will take proportionately longer.</li></ol> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40124?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '095148E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Within this combined degree program, students study a combination of Arts and Law courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Arts degree. In the final two years of the combined… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1cyxpk8-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Within this combined degree program, students study a combination of Arts and Law courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Arts degree. In the final two years of the combined degree program students complete the requirements of the Bachelor of Laws (Honours)and may enrol in these two years on a less than full time basis.</p> <p>Students completing this combined degree meet the requirements to practise law in NSW, and acquire skills and knowledge through the Arts studies they have chosen. You can major or minor in the following Arts areas (C - Callaghan campus, O - Ourimbah campus): - Aboriginal Studies (C) - Ancient History and Classical Languages (C) - Chinese (C)(Minor only. The Chinese major is available to pre-2012 continuing students only.) - Creative and Performing Arts (C, O) - English and Writing (C, O) - Film, Media and Cultural Studies (C, Flexible Delivery) - French Studies (C) - German (C) - History (C, O) - Human Geography and the Environment (C) - Japanese Studies (C) - Linguistics (C) - Philosophy and Religion (C) - Politics and International Relations (C, O) - Psychology Studies (C, O) - Sociology and Anthropology (C, O).</p> <p>Students wishing to practise law must also complete postgraduate professional training approved by the Legal Profession Admission Board. Alternatively, students completing this degree may apply for entry to the Bachelor of Laws (Honours)/Diploma of Legal Practice Program - see separate handbook entry - which allows immediate admission to legal practice on graduation.</p> <p>Commencement in this program is only available in Semester 1. Due to timetabling issues this program is not available for a Semester 2 commencement.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Arts/Bachelor of Laws (Honours) is undertaken over five years of full-time study. To satisfy the requirements of both degrees, students must complete 400 units of study comprising 160 units of Bachelor of Arts courses and 240 units of LAWS courses from the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) degree.</p> <p>In order to qualify for the Bachelor of Arts award, a student must pass 240 units comprising of 160 units of approved Bachelor of Arts courses and 80 units of LAWS courses as listed.</p> <p>The 160 units of approved Bachelor of Arts courses must successfully be completed in accordance with one of the following structures as set out in the Bachelor of Arts program handbook:</p> <p>1) double major option - one 80 unit Major + a second 80 unit Major;</p> <p>or</p> <p>2) Single Major and Double Minor Option - One 80 unit Major + One 40 unit Minor + A second 40 unit Minor.</p> <p>Please note: Your final transcript will not specify completed minors.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12340?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Within this combined degree program, students study a combination of Arts and Law courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Arts degree. In the final two years of the combined… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1wbz705-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Within this combined degree program, students study a combination of Arts and Law courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Arts degree. In the final two years of the combined degree program students complete the requirements of the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) and may enrol in these two years on a less than full time basis.</p> <p>Students who complete this combined degree acquire skills and knowledge through the Arts studies they have chosen, and then complete the Diploma of Legal Practice offered in the student’s fourth and fifth years, meet both the academic and practical training requirements to practice law in NSW. You can choose majors/minors in the following course areas (subject to change):</p> <p><strong>Majors and Minors:</strong></p> <ul><li>English &amp; Writing</li><li>Screen and Cultural Studies</li><li>French Studies (either Beginner or Intermediate Sequence)</li><li>Global Indigenous Studies</li><li>History</li><li>Human Geography &amp; the Environment</li><li>International Relations </li><li>Japanese Studies (either Beginner or Intermediate Sequence)</li><li>Linguistics</li><li>Performing Arts</li><li>Psychology Studies</li><li>Sociology &amp; Anthropology</li></ul> <p><strong>Minors only:</strong></p> <ul><li>Ancient History</li><li>Chinese</li><li>Education</li><li>Gender and Sexuality Studies</li><li>Information Technology</li><li>Studies of Philosophy, Religion and Ethics </li><li>Violence Studies</li><li>Writing Studies</li></ul> <p>After completing the Bachelor of Arts, students are automatically transferred into the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-laws-honours-diploma-of-legal-practice" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank">Bachelor of Laws (Honours)/Diploma of Legal Practice Program</a> for their fourth and fifth years of study. To opt out of this automatic transfer, students are required to contact <a href="mailto:programadvice@newcastle.edu.au" rel="nofollow">programadvice@newcastle.edu.au</a>. </p> <p>Students in the accredited Diploma of Legal Practice Program complete legal practice modules and practical legal training at the University of Newcastle Legal Centre and in placements with external organisations. </p> <p>Domestic students who commence full time in Semester 2 should expect to complete the program in a minimum of 5.5 years.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum selection rank, or satisfying the requirements for an approved admission scheme.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Arts/Bachelor of Laws (Honours) requires students to successfully complete 400 units, which is comprised of: </p> <ul><li>30 units Arts core courses; </li><li>160 units of Laws (Honours) core courses;</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement course list; </li><li>80 units of Laws (Honours) courses chosen from the course list; </li><li>One 80 unit Arts major; and</li><li>40 units of electives OR a 40 unit Arts minor.</li></ul> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 400 units. </p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '023104B';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Arts / Bachelor of Science is for those who are interested in understanding the world around us and how it works. Through the sciences you will be inspired to build new knowledge and discover new things. Through the arts you will explore ideas, theories and records of… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1lce01w-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Arts / Bachelor of Science is for those who are interested in understanding the world around us and how it works. Through the sciences you will be inspired to build new knowledge and discover new things. Through the arts you will explore ideas, theories and records of how people process the human experience through society, culture, and more. You’ll be able to follow your passions, and you will learn from leading researchers who will guide you through a tailored program, specifically designed to give you the skills that employers are seeking. Our guidance and mentoring give you the confidence to know you’re heading where you want to with your career, and you’ll have authentic opportunities to work with industry and in research whilst you study. A combined degree program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained in each separate degree. On completion, you will have the practical skills to make a difference in the world and contribute new solutions to the many challenges we face.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum selection rank, or satisfying the requirements for an approved admission scheme.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Arts/Bachelor of Science requires students to pass courses totalling 320 units, as follows:</p> <ul><li>50 units of Core Courses</li><li>10 unit Mathematics Course</li><li>10 unit Statistics Course List</li><li>10 unit Career-ready Placement Course</li><li>80 unit Major from the Bachelor of Arts</li><li>80* unit Major from the Bachelor of Science (except for Physics - 120 units)</li><li>80* units of Electives</li></ul> <p><strong>Notes</strong></p> <p>1) *Students can use 40 units of their Electives in order to complete the 120 unit Physics Major for their Bachelor of Science Major OR to complete a 40 unit Minor from the Bachelor of Arts.</p> <p>2) Students must only complete courses that form part of the program.</p> <p>3) Electives include any unrestricted courses offered within the university.</p> <p>4) Students choose the MATH course from the course list based on previous mathematical background. See the course descriptions for details.</p> <p>5) Students cannot complete both the Bachelor of Science Psychology Major and the Bachelor of Arts Psychology Science Major.</p> <p>6) Students cannot complete both the Bachelor of Science Geography Major and the Bachelor of Arts Human Geography and the Environment Major.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '098540F';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Graduates are trained in basic knowledge of the structure and function of living organisms with particular focus on the human. Using this knowledge, together with problem solving skills, critical reasoning and scientific methods taught in the program, the graduate is well prepared to collaborate on scientific investigations of human structure… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-t1m3cu-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Graduates are trained in basic knowledge of the structure and function of living organisms with particular focus on the human. Using this knowledge, together with problem solving skills, critical reasoning and scientific methods taught in the program, the graduate is well prepared to collaborate on scientific investigations of human structure and function in health and disease at a molecular, cellular and whole systems level.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '3 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Qualification for the award of Bachelor of Biomedical Science requires the completion of 240 units. Students must complete 160 units of core courses, 20 units from the career-ready placement course list, 50 units selected from the course list, and 10 units of electives. </p> <p>Please check the Bachelor of Biomedical Science Canvas site for course suggestions for students wishing to follow a research pathway, laboratory medicine pathway or clinical pathway. Note that the research pathway requires the elective course to be completed in semester 1 of Year 3.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40097?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '023110D';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Students who achieve a superior level of performance in the Bachelor of Biomedical Science at this university or any other degree approved by the College Board will be able to undertake the Honours program which is of one year''s duration when undertaken full-time. The Honours degree program allows students to… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1txavqy-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Students who achieve a superior level of performance in the Bachelor of Biomedical Science at this university or any other degree approved by the College Board will be able to undertake the Honours program which is of one year''s duration when undertaken full-time. The Honours degree program allows students to further develop their skills in Biomedical Science by undertaking a specific research project under the supervision of appropriate staff. <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/school/biomedical-sciences-and-pharmacy/research" rel="nofollow">Further information on research</a> can be found at the School of Biomedical Sciences and Pharmacy.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '1 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants having completed a Bachelor degree in a cognate area with a minimum GPA of 5.0:</p> <ul> <li>across all studies undertaken within the program; or</li> <li>across a major in the proposed area of study; or</li> <li>across 80 units of 3000 level courses (which must include at least 40 units of 3000 level courses in the major where a major exists); or</li> <li>where the applicant has completed less than 80 units at 3000 level, a GPA of 5.0 calculated from at least 60 units of 3000 level courses (which includes at least 40 units of 3000 level courses in the major where a major exists).</li> </ul> <p><strong> </strong>In exceptional circumstances, an application which does not meet the above requirements may be considered.</p> <p>Domestic applicants should apply using the direct <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/apply/end_on_honours">End-On Honours online application form</a>.</p> <p>International applicants should apply using the direct International <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions">application portal</a>. For more information see <a href="https://askuon-future.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/419/kw/international%20applicant">How do I apply as an International Student?</a></p> <p>You will also need to download and complete the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0007/86749/Bachelor-of-Biomedical-Science-Honours-Application-Form.pdf">Bachelor of Biomedical Science (Honours) Application form (PDF)</a> and attach it to your application. Only projects that have been pre-approved by the Honours Committee will be able to be used as the ‘Proposed Project’ on the forms.</p> <p>Information is now available for the <strong><a href="http://www.newcastle.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0004/1088545/List-of-approved-Biomed-Honours-projects-for-Sem-1-2026.pdf">2026 Biomedical Science Honours Projects</a></strong>. </p> <p></p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Biomedical Science (Honours) program is an academic extension of the Bachelor of Biomedical Science program. Students select a project from the range offered and undertake a research program specialising in a particular discipline from among the biomedical sciences.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10988?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '039702D';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Graduates are trained in basic knowledge of the structure and function of living organisms with particular focus on the human. Using this knowledge, together with problem solving skills, critical reasoning and scientific methods taught in the program, the graduate is well prepared to collaborate on scientific investigations of human structure… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-t1m3cu-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Graduates are trained in basic knowledge of the structure and function of living organisms with particular focus on the human. Using this knowledge, together with problem solving skills, critical reasoning and scientific methods taught in the program, the graduate is well prepared to collaborate on scientific investigations of human structure and function in health and disease at a molecular, cellular and whole systems level. </p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '3 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>This program does not accept applications for admission. The Bachelor of Biomedicine is an exit award. </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Qualification for the award of Bachelor of Biomedicine requires the completion of 240 units. Students must complete:</p> <ul><li>160 units of core corses; and</li><li>80 units of electives, with no more than 40 units at the 1000 level.</li></ul> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40312?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '106659J';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Graduates of the Bachelor of Biomedicine are trained in basic knowledge of the structure and function of living organisms with particular focus on the human. Using this knowledge, together with problem solving skills, critical reasoning and scientific methods taught in the program, the graduate is well prepared to collaborate on… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-5sequ-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Graduates of the Bachelor of Biomedicine are trained in basic knowledge of the structure and function of living organisms with particular focus on the human. Using this knowledge, together with problem solving skills, critical reasoning and scientific methods taught in the program, the graduate is well prepared to collaborate on scientific investigations of human structure and function in health and disease at a molecular, cellular and whole systems level.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Laws (Honours) degree meets the academic requirements needed to gain admission to the practice of law in New South Wales. As well as providing the academic basis for admission to legal practice, law is now regarded as a useful general education, fostering understanding of how society functions, and developing skills of analytical and logical reasoning. During the first three years, combined degree students enrol in the courses offered by the School of Law and Justice as part of the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) (LLB (Hons)), as well as courses within other Schools to complete their degree taken in combination with the LLB(Hons). During the final two years they enrol in LAWS courses only.</p> <p>Students who complete this combined degree and then complete the Diploma of Legal Practice offered in the student’s fourth and fifth years, meet both the academic and practical training requirements to practice law in NSW.</p> <p>After completing the Bachelor of Biomedicine, students are automatically transferred into the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-laws-honours-diploma-of-legal-practice" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank">Bachelor of Laws (Honours)/Diploma of Legal Practice Program</a> for their fourth and fifth years of study. To opt out of this automatic transfer, students are required to contact <a href="mailto:programadvice@newcastle.edu.au" rel="nofollow">programadvice@newcastle.edu.au</a>. </p> <p>Students in the accredited Diploma of Legal Practice Program complete legal practice modules and practical legal training at the University of Newcastle Legal Centre and in placements with external organisations. </p> <p> </p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum selection rank, or satisfying the requirements for an approved admission scheme.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>To meet the requirements of the Bachelor of Biomedicine/Bachelor of Laws (Honours) students are required to complete 400 units as follows:</p> <ul><li>160 units of Core Biomedical Science courses</li><li>160 units of Core Law courses</li><li>80 units of Law courses from the course list</li></ul> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40280?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '106660E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Biotechnology harnesses the natural biochemical and genetic processes of living organisms for our own use. Right now we are using it in genetic engineering, human health, pharmaceuticals, plant and animal agriculture, food production, fuels and waste management. The diversity of jobs available in biotechnology continues to increase and it is… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-t1m3cu-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Biotechnology harnesses the natural biochemical and genetic processes of living organisms for our own use. Right now we are using it in genetic engineering, human health, pharmaceuticals, plant and animal agriculture, food production, fuels and waste management. The diversity of jobs available in biotechnology continues to increase and it is expected to become one of the growth areas of the 21st Century.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '3 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Students are required to complete a total of, but no more than, 240 units, comprised of the following:</p> <ul><li>200 units of core courses</li><li>20 units of chemistry courses from the course list</li><li>10 unit mathematics course from the course list</li><li>10 unit elective</li></ul> <p>In addition, the program must also include:</p> <ul><li>No more than 100 units at 1000 level.</li><li>At least 40 units at 2000 level.</li><li>At least 60 units at 3000 level.</li></ul> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10981?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '059879B';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Biotechnology (Honours) is a one year full-time (or equivalent part-time) program that allows students to further develop their specific areas of interest. This degree prepares students for careers in biotechnology as well as providing a pathway into Research Higher Degree studies.</div><div aria-hidden="false" class="unset css-1knasfq-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Biotechnology (Honours) is a one year full-time (or equivalent part-time) program that allows students to further develop their specific areas of interest. This degree prepares students for careers in biotechnology as well as providing a pathway into Research Higher Degree studies.</p></div></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '1 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants having completed a Bachelor degree in a cognate area within the last five years with a minimum GPA of 5.0:</p> <ul> <li>across all studies undertaken within the program; or</li> <li>across a major in the proposed area of study; or</li> <li>across 80 units of 3000 level courses (which must include at least 40 units of 3000 level courses in the major where a major exists); or</li> <li>where the applicant has completed less than 80 units at 3000 level, a GPA of 5.5 calculated from at least 60 units of 3000 level courses (which includes at least 40 units of 3000 level courses in the major where a major exists).</li> </ul> <p>In exceptional circumstances, an application which does not meet the above requirements may be considered.</p> <p>Domestic applicants should apply using the direct <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/apply/end_on_honours">End-On Honours online application form</a>.</p> <p>International applicants should apply using the direct International <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions">application portal</a>. For more information see <a href="https://askuon-future.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/419/kw/international%20applicant">How do I apply as an International Student?</a></p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Honours program is normally undertaken over one year of full-time study or two years part-time.</p> <p>Students are required to complete 80 units to fulfil the requirements of the program.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10982?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '064596D';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Business equips students for the ever-evolving professional landscape by providing them a comprehensive range of applied skills and knowledge necessary to thrive as future business leaders. This program offers an applied approach to business education, encompassing crucial areas such as innovation, business analytics, marketing, management, and finance.… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-lks4f8-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Business equips students for the ever-evolving professional landscape by providing them a comprehensive range of applied skills and knowledge necessary to thrive as future business leaders. This program offers an applied approach to business education, encompassing crucial areas such as innovation, business analytics, marketing, management, and finance. Furthermore, students have the opportunity to delve deeper into their areas of interest through a selection of majors and minors. The six distinctive majors available within the program cater to diverse career aspirations, specifically: innovation and entrepreneurship, marketing, leadership and management, human resources management, international relations, and international business. Students can choose up to two majors, or instead undertake one major and up to two minors, providing skills across three areas of business.</p> <p>To ensure graduates are life-ready, the program places a strong emphasis on practical and applied learning. Case studies in the program are drawn from real-world business scenarios to provide students with a tangible understanding of the challenges and opportunities they may encounter in their careers. Authentic assessments further reinforce their ability to apply knowledge in a practical context. This combination of theory and hands-on experience equips students with a well-rounded skill set, enabling them to step into the dynamic business world with confidence and competence.</p> <p>All majors are available for study at Newcastle City Precinct.</p> <p>Majors offered at Ourimbah are: Marketing, Human Resource Management, Leadership and Management.</p> <p>Majors offered at PSB Singapore are: Marketing, Leadership and Management and International Business.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '3 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business requires students to successfully complete 240 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>60 units of Core Courses;</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement Course List;</li><li>10 units from the Business Course List;</li><li>And one of the following pathways: <ul><li>Pathway A: two 80 unit Business majors.</li><li>Pathway B: one 80 unit Business major and two 40 unit Business minors.</li><li>Pathway C: one 80 unit Business major, one 40 unit Business minor and 40 units of electives.</li><li>Pathway D: one 80 unit Business major and 80 units of electives.</li><li>Pathway E: one 80 unit Business major and one 80 unit Commerce major*.</li></ul> </li></ul> <p>Noting, for students who undertake a minor pathway, the choice in minor must be different from chosen major.</p> <p>*Pathway E Commerce major information:<br/>For students who undertake the Accounting major they must also take ECON111 from the Business Course List to be eligible for accreditation with CPA Australia, CA Australia and New Zealand, Association of Chartered Accountants (ACCA) and Association of International Accountants (AIA)</p> <p>Students must not exceed 100 units at 1000 level. </p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 240 units.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '001133A';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Business is a three year full-time (or equivalent part-time) program which starts with broad core courses and then progresses to one of the seven major sequences of study offered in the degree: Entrepreneurship and Innovation;Politics and International Relations;Human Resource Management;International Business;Leadership and Management;Marketing;Tourism and Event Management. The… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-18nu28r-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Business is a three year full-time (or equivalent part-time) program which starts with broad core courses and then progresses to one of the seven major sequences of study offered in the degree:</p> <ul><li>Entrepreneurship and Innovation;</li><li>Politics and International Relations;</li><li>Human Resource Management;</li><li>International Business;</li><li>Leadership and Management;</li><li>Marketing;</li><li>Tourism and Event Management.</li></ul> <p>The program has a practical orientation, with students learning from case studies of real business situations.</p> <p>All majors are available for study at Newcastle City. Majors offered at Ourimbah are Human Resource Management, Leadership and Management, and Marketing.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '3 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum selection rank, or satisfying the requirements for an approved admission scheme.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business requires students to successfully complete 240 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>70 units of core courses; </li><li>One 70 unit major (10 units of Core courses also count towards the major for a total of 80 units)</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement course list;</li><li>90 units of electives; and</li><li>PSB Singapore students will take 100 units of electives.</li></ul> <p>Students must complete a minimum of 40 units at each level (1000, 2000, 3000). </p> <p>Students must not exceed 100 units at 1000 level. </p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 240 units. </p> <p><strong>Majors</strong></p> <p>Students must complete at least one major sequence to fulfil the requirements of their program. Some core courses may count towards specific majors as listed below. </p> <p>Students may utilise their elective courses to undertake a double major. Students must ensure that each major has 60 units of unique courses.</p> <p><strong>Entrepreneurship and Innovation</strong></p> <p>Core course LEGL1001 counts towards this major. To fulfil the requirements of this major, students must complete 40 units of compulsory courses and 30 units from the course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level). When selecting elective courses, students must ensure to select a minimum of 10 units at the 3000 level. </p> <p><strong>Politics and International Relations</strong></p> <p>Core course LEGL1001 counts towards this major. To fulfil the requirements of this major, students must complete 20 units of compulsory courses and 50 units from the course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 1000 level and 10 units at the 2000 level).</p> <p><strong>Human Resource Management</strong></p> <p>Core course MNGT1001 counts towards this major. To fulfil the requirements of this major, students must complete 50 units of compulsory courses and 20 units from the course list. </p> <p><strong>International Business</strong></p> <p>Core course MNGT1001 counts towards this major. To fulfil the requirements of this major, students must complete 40 units of compulsory courses and 30 units from the course list. </p> <p><strong>Leadership and Management </strong></p> <p>Core course MNGT1001 counts towards this major. To fulfil the requirements of this major, students must complete 30 units of compulsory courses and 40 units from the course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level). </p> <p><strong>Marketing</strong></p> <p>Core course MKTG1001 counts towards this major. To fulfil the requirements of this major, students must complete 30 units of compulsory courses and 40 units from the course lists. </p> <p><strong>Tourism and Event Management</strong></p> <p>Core course MNGT1001 counts towards this major. To fulfil the requirements of this major, students must complete 40 units of compulsory courses and 30 units from the course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level). </p> <p>All majors are available for study at Newcastle City. Majors offered at Ourimbah are Human Resource Management, Leadership and Management, and Marketing. </p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '001133A';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Students who perform well, with a GPA of 5.0 or greater, during the Bachelor of Business program or equivalent program may undertake a further year of full-time (or equivalent part-time) study to obtain an Honours degree. The Honours program allows students to further develop their specific areas of interest. Students… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1nicxnb-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Students who perform well, with a GPA of 5.0 or greater, during the Bachelor of Business program or equivalent program may undertake a further year of full-time (or equivalent part-time) study to obtain an Honours degree. The Honours program allows students to further develop their specific areas of interest.</p> <p>Students can undertake the Honours program in one of the following discipline areas:</p> <ul><li>Innovation and Entrepreneurship</li><li>Marketing</li><li>Leadership and Management</li><li>Human Resource Management </li><li>International Relations</li><li>International Business</li></ul> <p>Potential Honours students should consult with the Newcastle Business School towards the end of the semester prior to that in which they intend to enrol.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '1 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants having completed a Bachelor degree in a cognate area with a minimum GPA of 5.0:</p> <ul> <li>across all studies undertaken within the program; or</li> <li>across a major in the proposed area of study; or</li> <li>across 80 units of 3000 level courses (which must include at least 40 units of 3000 level courses in the major where a major exists); or</li> <li>where the applicant has completed less than 80 units at 3000 level, a GPA of 5.0 calculated from at least 60 units of 3000 level courses (which includes at least 40 units of 3000 level courses in the major where a major exists).</li> </ul> <p>In exceptional circumstances, an application which does not meet the above requirements may be considered.</p> <p>Domestic applicants should apply using the direct <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/apply/end_on_honours">End-On Honours online application form</a>.</p> <p>International applicants should apply using the direct International <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions">application portal</a>. For more information see <a href="https://askuon-future.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/419/kw/international%20applicant">How do I apply as an International Student?</a></p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>This program requires the successful completion of 80 units of core courses. </p> <p>Students undertake the Honours program from one of the following discipline areas:</p> <ul><li>Innovation and Entrepreneurship</li><li>Marketing</li><li>Leadership and Management</li><li>Human Resource Management</li><li>International Relations</li><li>International Business</li></ul> <p>Students who wish to complete the Honours program in two discipline areas should apply to the Program Convenor.</p> <p>Course supervisory arrangements will be flexible across campus locations and/or zoom where appropriate.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11060?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '030569K';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Business Analytics focuses on emergent issues in context specific domains within business, preparing students to think like business decision makers who understand how business analytics supports the business decision making process. This program provides domain specific context and knowledge from a range of business disciplines and utilises… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1txavqy-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Business Analytics focuses on emergent issues in context specific domains within business, preparing students to think like business decision makers who understand how business analytics supports the business decision making process. This program provides domain specific context and knowledge from a range of business disciplines and utilises cases to provide students opportunities to apply new knowledge to resolve prolbems and issues that they will encounter in business contexts.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '3 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business Analytics requires students to successfully complete 240 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>110 units of Core Courses;</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement Course List;</li><li>80 units from the Business Analytics Course List; and</li><li>40 units of electives.</li></ul> <p>Students must complete a minimum of 40 units at each level (1000, 2000, 3000). </p> <p>Students must not exceed 100 units at 1000 level. </p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 240 units.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40263?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '102641G';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">This combined degree program provides students with the opportunity to increase the depth and breadth of their study in relevant disciplines within Business and Business Analytics whilst completing two awards over four years of full-time study or part-time equivalent. A combined degree program enhances the academic and professional qualities gained… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1txavqy-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>This combined degree program provides students with the opportunity to increase the depth and breadth of their study in relevant disciplines within Business and Business Analytics whilst completing two awards over four years of full-time study or part-time equivalent.</p> <p>A combined degree program enhances the academic and professional qualities gained in each separate degree. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Business Analytics requires students to successfully complete 320 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>140 units of core courses;</li><li>One 70 unit Business major (10 units of Core courses also count towards the major for a total of 80 units);</li><li>10 units of courses from the course list;</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement course list; and</li><li>90 units of electives.</li></ul> <p>Students must not exceed a maximum of 100 units at any level in each of the component programs.</p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 320 units. </p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40264?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '102642F';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">This combined degree program provides students with the opportunity to increase the depth and breadth of their study in relevant disciplines within Business and Commerce whilst completing two awards over four years of full-time study or part-time equivalent. A combined degree program enhances the academic and professional qualities gained in… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1lce01w-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>This combined degree program provides students with the opportunity to increase the depth and breadth of their study in relevant disciplines within Business and Commerce whilst completing two awards over four years of full-time study or part-time equivalent.</p> <p>A combined degree program enhances the academic and professional qualities gained in each separate degree. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills.</p> <p>Students should refer to the separate program handbook entries for specific information about the programs. Bachelor of Business: <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-business/handbook" rel="nofollow">https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-business/handbook </a> </p> <p>Bachelor of Commerce: <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-commerce/handbook" rel="nofollow">https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-commerce/handbook</a></p> <p> </p> <p> </p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Commerce requires students to successfully complete 320 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>90 units of core courses; </li><li>One 70 unit Bachelor of Business major (10 units of Core courses also count towards the major for a total of 80 units);</li><li>One 60 unit Bachelor of Commerce major (20 units of Core courses also count towards the major for a total of 80 units);</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement Course list; and</li><li>90 units of electives. </li></ul> <p>Students must not exceed a maximum of 100 units at any level in each of the component programs.</p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 320 units. </p> <p>Students may utilise their elective courses to undertake a double major. Students must ensure that each major has 60 units of unique courses.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '029749E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">This combined degree program provides students with the opportunity to increase the depth and breadth of their study in relevant disciplines within Business and Commerce whilst completing two awards over four years of full-time study or part-time equivalent. The Bachelor of Business equips students for the ever-evolving professional landscape by… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1s1c2em-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>This combined degree program provides students with the opportunity to increase the depth and breadth of their study in relevant disciplines within Business and Commerce whilst completing two awards over four years of full-time study or part-time equivalent. The Bachelor of Business equips students for the ever-evolving professional landscape by providing them a comprehensive range of applied skills and knowledge necessary to thrive as future business leaders. The Bachelor of Commerce is designed to empower students with contemporary theoretical, technical, and practical business knowledge and life-ready skills which is a stepping stone for becoming a fully qualified accountant or undertaking a career in finance and economics.</p> <p>A combined degree program enhances the academic and professional qualities gained in each separate degree. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills within the domain of business and related fields.</p> <p>Students will undertake one major in each program.</p> <p>Business majors:</p> <ul><li>Innovation and Entrepreneurship</li><li>Marketing</li><li>Leadership and Management</li><li>Human Resources Management</li><li>International Relations</li><li>International Business</li></ul> <p>Commerce majors:</p> <ul><li>Accounting</li><li>Economics</li><li>Finance</li></ul> <p>All majors are available for study at Newcastle City.</p> <p>Majors offered at Ourimbah:</p> <ul><li>Accounting</li><li>Marketing</li><li>Leadership and Management</li></ul> <p><em><strong>Greater Bank Finance Lab</strong> - Located on level one of NUspace, the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/school/newcastle-business-school/greater-bank-finance-lab" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="target">Greater Bank Finance Lab</a> is a hands-on learning environment, enabling Newcastle Business School students to build their skills in financial decision making, risk management and economic systems, before they graduate.</em> </p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Commerce requires students to successfully complete 320 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>70 units core courses;</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement course list;</li><li>80 unit Business major;</li><li>80 unit Commerce major; and</li><li>80 units of electives.</li></ul> <p>Students must not exceed a maximum of 100 units at any level in each of the component programs.</p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 320 units. </p> <p>Students may utilise their elective courses to undertake a double major. Students must ensure that each major has 60 units of unique courses.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '029749E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Innovation and Entrepreneurship (BBUS/BIE) is a 320 unit program offered on a full-time (or equivalent part-time) basis. The program starts with broad core courses and then progresses to one of six major sequences of study offered in the degree: Politics and International Relations;Human Resource Management;International… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-16j67wv-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Innovation and Entrepreneurship (BBUS/BIE) is a 320 unit program offered on a full-time (or equivalent part-time) basis. The program starts with broad core courses and then progresses to one of six major sequences of study offered in the degree:</p> <ul><li>Politics and International Relations;</li><li>Human Resource Management;</li><li>International Business;</li><li>Leadership and Management;</li><li>Marketing;</li><li>Tourism and Event Management.</li></ul></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Innovation and Entrepreneurship requires students to successfully complete 320 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>160 units of core courses; </li><li>One 70 unit Business major (10 units of Core courses also count towards the major for a total of 80 units); <ul><li>Please note the Entrepreneurship and Innovation major is not available to students studying this combined degree.</li></ul> </li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement course list; and</li><li>80 units of electives. </li></ul> <p>Students must not exceed a maximum of 100 units at any level in each of the component programs.</p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 320 units. </p> <p>Students may utilise their elective courses to undertake a double major. Students must ensure that each major has 60 units of unique courses. </p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40016?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Within the combined degree program, students study a combination of Bachelor of Business and Bachelor of Laws (Honours) courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Business degree. In the final… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-18nu28r-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Within the combined degree program, students study a combination of Bachelor of Business and Bachelor of Laws (Honours) courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Business degree. In the final two years of the combined degree program students complete the requirements for the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) and may enrol in these two years on a less than full time basis.</p> <p>Students completing this combined degree program become specialists in Business and meet the academic requirements to practice law in NSW. However, students wishing to practice law must also complete postgraduate professional training approved by the Legal Profession Admission Board. Alternatively, students completing this degree may apply for entry to the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) /Diploma of Legal Practice Program - see separate handbook entry - which allows immediate admission to legal practice on graduation.</p> <p>Domestic students who commence full time in Semester 2 should expect to complete the program in a minimum of 5.5 years.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum selection rank, or satisfying the requirements for an approved admission scheme.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p> </p> <p> </p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <p> </p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Laws (Honours) is undertaken over five years of full-time study. The combined degree program requires successful completion of 400 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>60 units Business core courses;</li><li>160 units Laws (Honours) core courses;</li><li>80 units Laws (Honours) courses chosen from the course list;</li><li>One 70 unit Business major (10 units of Core courses also count towards some majors for a total of 80 units); </li><li>10 units from the Work Integrated Learning course list; and</li><li>20 units of electives. </li></ul> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 400 units. </p> <p>Please note combined Law students receive an exemption for LEGL1001 in the Business degree. </p> <p>Students studying the Human Resource Management major undertake LAWS6024 Employment Law rather than LEGL3111.</p> <p>Credit towards the Bachelor of Business degree is granted for the 80 units of the Bachelor of Laws courses taken in the first three years, taking the total Bachelor of Business units to 240. On successful completion of the first three years of the combined degree program outlined above, you will have completed all the required courses for the Bachelor of Business degree.</p> <p>To meet the requirements for the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) degree you must complete 240 units, including 160 units of Core Laws courses and 80 units Laws courses chosen from the course list.</p> <p>Students studying the Human Resource Management major cannot count LAWS6024 Employment Law as part of the 80 units of LAWS courses chosen from the course list. </p> <p>The final two years of the combined degree program comprises of study in LAWS courses only. </p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '032796E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Within the combined degree program, students study a combination of Bachelor of Business and Bachelor of Laws (Honours) courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Business degree. In the final… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-18kj5j0-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Within the combined degree program, students study a combination of Bachelor of Business and Bachelor of Laws (Honours) courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Business degree. In the final two years of the combined degree program students complete the requirements for the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) and may enrol in these two years on a less than full time basis.</p> <p>Students who complete this combined degree program become specialists in Business and Law, and then complete the Diploma of Legal Practice offered in the student’s fourth and fifth years, meet both the academic and practical training requirements to practice law in NSW.</p> <p>After completing the Bachelor of Business, students are automatically transferred into the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-laws-honours-diploma-of-legal-practice" rel="nofollow">Bachelor of Laws (Honours)/Diploma of Legal Practice Program</a> for their fourth and fifth years of study. To opt out of this automatic transfer, students are required to contact <a href="mailto:programadvice@newcastle.edu.au" rel="nofollow">programadvice@newcastle.edu.au</a>. </p> <p>Students in the accredited Diploma of Legal Practice Program complete legal practice modules and practical legal training at the University of Newcastle Legal Centre and in placements with external organisations. </p> <p>Domestic students who commence full time in Semester 2 should expect to complete the program in a minimum of 5.5 years.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Laws (Honours) requires students to successfully complete 400 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>220 units of Core Courses;</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement Course List;</li><li>10 units from the Business Course List;</li><li>80 units from the Law Course list; and</li><li>One 80 unit Bachelor of Business major. </li></ul> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 400 units.</p> <p>Credit towards the Bachelor of Business degree is granted for the 80 units of the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) courses taken in the first three years, taking the total Bachelor of Business units to 240. On successful completion of the first three years of the combined degree program outlined above, you will have completed all the required courses for the Bachelor of Business degree.</p> <p>To meet the requirements for the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) degree you must complete 240 units, including 160 units of Core Laws courses and 80 units Laws courses chosen from the course list. The final two years of the combined degree program comprises of study in LAWS courses only. </p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '032796E';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The combined Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Media Communication program is an interdisciplinary degree designed to equip students with a wide range of skills and knowledge necessary to thrive in the dynamic and ever-changing professional landscape. This program combines the applied approach of the Bachelor of Business with the global industry… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-mj5o60-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The combined Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Media Communication program is an interdisciplinary degree designed to equip students with a wide range of skills and knowledge necessary to thrive in the dynamic and ever-changing professional landscape. This program combines the applied approach of the Bachelor of Business with the global industry perspective of the Bachelor of Media Communication, providing students with a unique blend of business acumen and communication expertise.</p> <p>In the Bachelor of Business component, students gain a comprehensive and practical understanding of crucial business areas such as innovation, business analytics, marketing, management, and finance. The six distinctive majors available within the degree cater to diverse career aspirations, specifically: innovation and entrepreneurship, marketing, leadership and management, human resources management, international relations, and international business.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Media and Communication component prepares students to create text, vision, and sound-based content for different purposes and for a variety of organisations, individuals, and institutions. Students learn to connect theory and practice, collaborate with local and global communities, and effect positive change by creating and designing industry-relevant solutions to important societal and global issues. The three media and communication majors available are: Media Production, News Media, and Public Relations.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Media and Communication requires students to successfully complete 320 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>130 units of Core Courses;</li><li>10 units from the Career-ready placement Course List;</li><li>10 units from the Business Course List;</li><li>One 80 unit Business major;</li><li>One 80 unit Media and Communication major; and </li><li>10 units of electives. </li></ul> <p>Students must not exceed a maximum of 100 units at any level in each of the component programs.</p> <p>Students must only complete courses that form part of the program and must not complete more than 320 units.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50048?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '116624D';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Chemical engineering is at the forefront of efforts to address the most significant issues facing the international community in the 21st Century: the provision of potable water, overcoming greenhouse gas emissions, and the establishment of clean energy sources. Chemical engineering is concerned with the processing of gases, liquids and solids… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-lfwx49-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Chemical engineering is at the forefront of efforts to address the most significant issues facing the international community in the 21st Century: the provision of potable water, overcoming greenhouse gas emissions, and the establishment of clean energy sources. Chemical engineering is concerned with the processing of gases, liquids and solids for the purpose of producing everyday products from toothpaste to steel. Chemical engineers also apply their skills to solving problems in many fields including the emerging fields of biotechnology, microfluids and nanotechnology and the environmental sector.</p> <p>All University of Newcastle engineering students must complete 12-weeks of industrial experience. During your industrial experience, you will build important professional networks and put your learning into practice.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum selection rank, or satisfying the requirements for an approved admission scheme.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours) is a four year program, students are required to complete 320 units, which is comprised of: </p> <ul><li>280 units of Core courses; and</li><li>0-unit compulsory Industrial Experience</li><li>40 units of Elective courses.</li></ul> <p>No more than 120 units can be taken at 1000 level; and at least 40 units must be taken at each level from the 2000 level and above for this program. </p> <p><strong>Elective Pathway</strong></p> <p>An Elective pathway gives students the opportunity to broaden their skills and knowledge in their own or another engineering discipline; or specialise in areas such as business, maths or science; or undertake study overseas. Please be aware of the 120 unit maximum for 1000 level courses in your program when selecting your elective pathway.</p> <p><strong>Mathematics Pathways</strong></p> <p>Students who do not meet the enrolment requisite for MATH1110 must take MATH1002 Foundational Studies in Mathematics. For these students MATH1002 will count for 10 units of electives. Students undertaking this pathway will need to be aware of the 1000 level unit restrictions when enrolling in their remaining elective courses.</p> <p><strong>Physics Pathways</strong></p> <p>Students may count PHYS1205 in lieu of PHYS1210 with Program Convenor approval. </p> <ul><li>Students wishing to undertake this program on a part-time basis are advised to contact the Program Convenor or Program Advisor (ProgramAdvice@newcastle.edu.au) for advice on optimum selection of courses for part-time enrolment.</li><li>Please note that if you undertake courses that are not in your approved program, you will be liable for additional fees for those courses. This is in addition to the fees associated with your normal program of study.</li></ul> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40339?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '111298J';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Chemical engineering is at the forefront of efforts to address the most significant issues facing the international community in the 21st Century: the provision of potable water, overcoming greenhouse gas emissions, and the establishment of clean energy sources. Chemical engineering is concerned with the processing of gases, liquids and solids… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-avarg1-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Chemical engineering is at the forefront of efforts to address the most significant issues facing the international community in the 21st Century: the provision of potable water, overcoming greenhouse gas emissions, and the establishment of clean energy sources. Chemical engineering is concerned with the processing of gases, liquids and solids for the purpose of producing everyday products from toothpaste to steel. Chemical engineers also apply their skills to solving problems in many fields including the emerging fields of biotechnology, microfluids and nanotechnology and the environmental sector.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours) is a four year program, students are required to complete 320 units, which is comprised of: </p> <ul><li>280 units of core courses; and</li><li>40 units of elective courses.</li></ul> <p>No more than 120 units can be taken at 1000 level; and at least 40 units must be taken at each level from the 2000 level and above for this program. </p> <p><strong>Elective Pathway</strong></p> <p>An elective pathway gives students the opportunity to broaden their skills and knowledge in their own or another engineering discipline; or specialise in areas such as business, maths or science; or undertake study overseas. Please be aware of the 120 unit maximum for 1000 level courses in your program when selecting your elective pathway.</p> <p><strong>Mathematics Pathways</strong></p> <p>Students who do not meet the enrolment requisite for MATH1110 must take MATH1002 Foundational Studies in Mathematics. For these students MATH1002 will count for 10 units of electives. Students undertaking this pathway will need to be aware of the 1000 level unit restrictions when enrolling in their remaining elective courses.</p> <p><strong>Physics Pathways</strong></p> <p>Students may count PHYS1205 in lieu of PHYS1210 with Program Convenor approval. </p> <ul><li>Students wishing to undertake this program on a part-time basis are advised to contact the Program Convenor or Program Advisor (ProgramAdvice@newcastle.edu.au) for advice on optimum selection of courses for part-time enrolment.</li><li>Please note that if you undertake courses that are not in your approved program, you will be liable for additional fees for those courses. This is in addition to the fees associated with your normal program of study.</li></ul> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40055?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '018788M';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Business combined degree program provides students with an opportunity to undertake concurrent study and complete two awards. In general, the combined degree program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained in each degree. At the same time, it… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-t1m3cu-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Business combined degree program provides students with an opportunity to undertake concurrent study and complete two awards. In general, the combined degree program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained in each degree. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>For all combined programs and in accordance with the Program Management Procedure Manual - Coursework, the core and minimum requirements for each single degree component must be met in each combined program. This has been done economically, exploiting overlaps where possible, so that accreditation of either program is not compromised.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Business program is a five year program, students are required to complete a total of 410 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>340 units of core courses;</li><li>70 units towards a major (10 units of Core courses also count towards the major for a total of 80 units). Students may choose either: <ul><li>The Leadership and Management Major, made up of 30 units compulsory courses and 40 units from the course list; <em>or</em> </li><li>The Entrepreneurship and Innovation Major, made up of 40 units compulsory courses and 30 units from the course list.</li></ul> </li></ul> <p>Some core courses count towards specific majors as listed below.</p> <ul><li>LEGL1001 - Entrepreneurship and Innovation; Leadership and Management majors.</li><li>MNGT1001 - Leadership and Management major.</li></ul> <p><strong>Step-out Information</strong></p> <p>The program has a duration of 5 years full time (or part time equivalent). It is possible for a student to ''''step out'''' with a single degree award only and not complete the combined program they are enrolled in. In order to do this, a student would be required to complete all the single degree requirements for their preferred degree and may be required to complete any omitted courses that are not included in the combined degree.</p> <p>Omitted Courses:</p> <ul><li>Bachelor of Business core course <em>STAT1060 Business Decision Making (10 units)</em> has been omitted from the program.</li></ul> <p><strong>A student wishing to ''''step out'''' with a single degree from this combined program should contact their Program Convenor or Academic Program Advisor (ProgramAdvice@newcastle.edu.au) for further information. </strong> </p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40078?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Business combined degree program provides students with an opportunity to undertake concurrent study and complete two awards. In general, the combined degree program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained in each degree. At the same time, it… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1ifr8ht-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Business combined degree program provides students with an opportunity to undertake concurrent study and complete two awards. In general, the combined degree program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained in each degree. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills.</p> <p>All University of Newcastle engineering students must complete 12-weeks of industrial experience. During your industrial experience, you will build important professional networks and put your learning into practice.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum selection rank, or satisfying the requirements for an approved admission scheme.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>For all combined programs and in accordance with the Program Management Procedure Manual - Coursework, the Core and minimum requirements for each single degree component must be met in each combined program. This has been done economically, exploiting overlaps where possible, so that accreditation of either program is not compromised.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Business program is a five-year program, students are required to complete a total of 410 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>330 units of Core courses;</li><li>0-unit compulsory Industrial Experience;</li><li>80 units towards a Business major: <ul><li>Innovation and Entrepreneurship; or</li><li>Leadership and Management</li></ul> </li></ul> <p><strong>Step-out Information:</strong></p> <p>The program has a duration of 5 years full time (or part time equivalent). It is possible for a student to ''''step out'''' with a single degree award only and not complete the combined program they are enrolled in. In order to do this, a student would be required to complete all the single degree requirements for their preferred degree and may be required to complete any omitted courses that are not included in the combined degree.</p> <p><strong>Omitted Courses:</strong></p> <p>Bachelor of Business Core course BUSN1010 Analytics in Business (10 units) has been omitted from the program.</p> <p>A student wishing to ''''step out'''' with a single degree from this combined program should contact their Program Convenor or Program Advisor (ProgramAdvice@newcastle.edu.au) for further information. </p> <p><strong>Physics Pathways</strong></p> <p>Students may count PHYS1205 in lieu of PHYS1210 with Program Convenor approval.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40350?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '111299H';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/ Bachelor of Mathematics combined degree program provides students with an opportunity to undertake study in the fields of both chemical engineering and mathematics and complete two awards. In general, a combined program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-16j67wv-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/ Bachelor of Mathematics combined degree program provides students with an opportunity to undertake study in the fields of both chemical engineering and mathematics and complete two awards. In general, a combined program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained in each separate program. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills. Within this program, students have the opportunity to select some courses according to their individual areas of interest and also complete twelve weeks of industry experience. They will have the opportunity to undertake an industry-related engineering project in their final year of study.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">International Applicants</a></li> </ul> <p> </p> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>For all combined programs and in accordance with the Program Management Procedure Manual - Coursework, the core and minimum requirements for each single degree component must be met in each combined program. This has been done economically, exploiting overlaps where possible, so that accreditation of either program is not compromised.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Mathematics is a five year program, students are required to complete a total of 400 units, which is comprised of: </p> <ul><li>330 units of core courses; </li><li>60 units - Studies in Mathematics and Statistics Major (20 units from within the core contribute to make this major 80 units) made up of: <ul><li>20 units are taken at the 2000 level.</li><li>40 units are taken at the 3000 level; and</li></ul> </li><li>10 units of elective courses.</li></ul> <p>No more than 120 units can be taken at 1000 level; and at least 40 units must be taken at each level from the 2000 level and above for this program. </p> <p><strong>Step-out Information</strong></p> <p>The program has a duration of 5 years full time (or part time equivalent). It is possible for a student to ''''step out'''' with a single degree award only and not complete the combined program they are enrolled in. In order to do this, a student would be required to complete all the single degree requirements for their preferred degree and may be required to complete any omitted courses that are not included in the combined degree</p> <p>Omitted Courses:</p> <ul><li>Bachelor of Mathematics core course <em>STAT1100 Data Wrangling and Visualisation (10 units)</em> has been omitted from the program in lieu of core courses <em>ENGG1500 Introduction to Professional Engineering (10 units)</em> and <em>ENGG1003 Introduction to Procedural Programming (10 units).</em> </li></ul> <p><strong>A student wishing to ''''step out'''' with a single degree from this combined program should contact their Program Convenor or Academic Program Advisor (ProgramAdvice@newcastle.edu.au) for further information.</strong></p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40079?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/ Bachelor of Mathematics combined degree program provides students with an opportunity to undertake study in the fields of both chemical engineering and mathematics and complete two awards. In general, a combined program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1lce01w-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/ Bachelor of Mathematics combined degree program provides students with an opportunity to undertake study in the fields of both chemical engineering and mathematics and complete two awards. In general, a combined program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained in each separate program. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills. Within this program, students have the opportunity to select some courses according to their individual areas of interest and also complete twelve weeks of industry experience. They will have the opportunity to undertake an industry-related engineering project in their final year of study.</p> <p>All University of Newcastle engineering students must complete 12-weeks of industrial experience. During your industrial experience, you will build important professional networks and put your learning into practice.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
