UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Science combined degree program is offered by the College of Engineering, Science and Environment. This program provides students with the opportunity to undertake concurrent study in Chemical Engineering and Science with a major in Chemistry (Advanced Materials) and complete two awards. In general,… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1lce01w-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Science combined degree program is offered by the College of Engineering, Science and Environment. This program provides students with the opportunity to undertake concurrent study in Chemical Engineering and Science with a major in Chemistry (Advanced Materials) and complete two awards. In general, a combined degree program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained in each separate degree. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills.</p> <p>The Chemistry (Advanced Materials) major is the only Bachelor of Science major available in this program. </p> <p>All University of Newcastle engineering students must complete 12-weeks of industrial experience. During your industrial experience, you will build important professional networks and put your learning into practice.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '5 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>Admission to this program is available to Australian citizens and residents only.</p> <p>Eligibility for admission to this program is based on applicants meeting the minimum <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/selection-ranks-and-entry-schemes">selection rank</a>, or satisfying the requirements for an approved <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes">admission scheme</a>.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle accepts a range of qualifications to determine eligibility for admission. These include, but are not limited to, Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (such as the HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, and completed enabling programs.</p> <p>For further information on the pathways that are available to you, please refer to:</p> <ul> <li> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in">Domestic Applicants</a></p> </li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>For all combined programs and in accordance with the Program Management Procedure Manual - Coursework, the Core and minimum requirements for each single degree component must be met in each combined program. This has been done economically, exploiting overlaps where possible, so that accreditation of either program is not compromised.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Science program is a five year program, students are required to complete a total of 400 units, which is comprised of:</p> <ul><li>300 units of Core courses</li><li>60 units of courses for the Major (20 units of Core courses also count towards the major for a total of 80 units): <ul><li>30 units of compulsory courses</li><li>30 units chosen from the course list </li></ul> </li><li>0-unit compulsory Industrial Experience; and</li><li>40 units of Electives. </li></ul> <p>The Chemistry major is the only Bachelor of Science Major available in this program. </p> <p>No more than 120 units can be taken at 1000 level; and at least 40 units must be taken at each level from the 2000 level and above for this program. </p> <p><strong>Elective Pathway</strong></p> <p>An Elective pathway gives students the opportunity to broaden their skills and knowledge in their own or another engineering discipline; or specialise in areas such as business, maths or science; or undertake study overseas. Please be aware of the 120 unit maximum for 1000 level courses in your program when selecting your Elective pathway.</p> <p><strong>Step-out Information</strong></p> <p>The program has a duration of 5 years full time (or part time equivalent). It is possible for a student to ''''step out'''' with a single degree award only and not complete the combined program they are enrolled in. In order to do this, a student would be required to complete all the single degree requirements for their preferred degree and may be required to complete any omitted courses that are not included in the combined degree.Omitted Courses:</p> <ul><li>Bachelor of Science core course <em>STAT1070 Statistics for the Sciences (10 units)</em> has been omitted from the program in lieu of core course <em>STAT2110 Engineering Statistics (10 units). </em></li><li>Bachelor of Science core courses <em>SCIE3001A Transdisciplinary Capstone: Planning &amp; Implementing (10 units)</em> and <em>SCIE3001B Transdisciplinary Capstone: Implementing &amp; Communicating (10 units)</em> have been omitted from the program in lieu of core courses <em>CHEE4975A Chemical Engineering Research A (10 units)</em> and <em>CHEE4975B Chemical Engineering Research B (10 units)</em>.</li></ul> <p><strong>A student wishing to ''''step out'''' with a single degree from this combined program should contact their Program Convenor or Program Advisor (ProgramAdvice@newcastle.edu.au) for further information. </strong></p> <p><strong>Mathematics Pathways </strong></p> <p>Students who do not meet the enrolment requisite for MATH1110 must take MATH1002 Foundational Studies in Mathematics. For these students MATH1002 will count for 10 units of electives. Students undertaking this pathway will need to be aware of the 1000 level unit restrictions when enrolling in their remaining elective courses.</p> <p><strong>Physics Pathways</strong></p> <p>Students may count PHYS1205 in lieu of PHYS1210 with Program Convenor approval.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40352?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

