    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Science combined degree program is offered by the Faculty of Engineering and Built Environment and the Faculty of Science. This program provides students with the opportunity to undertake concurrent study in Chemical Engineering and Science with a major in Chemistry (Advanced Materials) and… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-16j67wv-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)/Bachelor of Science combined degree program is offered by the Faculty of Engineering and Built Environment and the Faculty of Science. This program provides students with the opportunity to undertake concurrent study in Chemical Engineering and Science with a major in Chemistry (Advanced Materials) and complete two awards. In general, a combined degree program offers greater breadth of learning, enhancing the academic and professional qualities gained in each separate degree. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills.</p> <p>The Chemistry (Advanced Materials) major is the only Bachelor of Science major available in this program.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-S