UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Undergraduate Certificate in Innovation and Entrepreneurship provides students with a purpose-driven, experiential learning pathway to develop core competencies in for example creativity, empathy, innovation, GenAI literacy, and human-centred problem solving. While the program may lead to the development of startups or social enterprises, its broader aim is to equip… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-o21fmn-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Undergraduate Certificate in Innovation and Entrepreneurship provides students with a purpose-driven, experiential learning pathway to develop core competencies in for example creativity, empathy, innovation, GenAI literacy, and human-centred problem solving. While the program may lead to the development of startups or social enterprises, its broader aim is to equip students with the mindset and capabilities to identify meaningful challenges and co-create impactful solutions.</p> <p>Delivered through four scaffolded courses, the program combines applied learning, collaborative project work, and the integration of Generative AI tools to enhance critical and creative thinking. Students will engage in challenge-based learning, research real-world problems, and prototype solutions in both local and global contexts. The program fosters collaboration—both human and AI-enabled—and encourages students to explore their entrepreneurial identity and build a portfolio of evidence demonstrating their progress.</p> <p>Designed as both a standalone qualification and a pathway into the Innovation and Entrepreneurship major, the undergraduate certificate supports students in making informed, ethical, and impactful contributions to their chosen field or community.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '0 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>To be eligible for admission to the program, applicants must have either:</p> <ol> <li>An unadjusted selection rank equivalent to 50 or above. This may be assessed on the basis of any qualification accepted by the University which includes (but is not limited to) Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (eg HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, or completed enabling programs; OR</li> <li>One or more years of full-time professional experience (or part-time equivalent) in a relevant field.</li> </ol> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Undergraduate Certificate in Innovation and Entrepreneurship is a 0.5 year part-time equivalent program requiring students to complete 40 units of core courses.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50111?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Undergraduate Certificate in Languages offers students the opportunity to gain a strong grounding in a language other than English, or to be introduced to a range of languages. The Undergraduate Certificate in Languages is available as a stand-alone qualification or as a concurrent enrolment alongside any undergraduate program. Students… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-avarg1-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Undergraduate Certificate in Languages offers students the opportunity to gain a strong grounding in a language other than English, or to be introduced to a range of languages. The Undergraduate Certificate in Languages is available as a stand-alone qualification or as a concurrent enrolment alongside any undergraduate program.</p> <p>Students will undertake 40 units of language courses. The Undergraduate Certificate in Languages is intended to be taken part-time to allow time for language acquisition, however a full-time enrolment is possible in semester 1 or 2.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '0 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>To be eligible for admission to the program, applicants must have either: </p> <ol> <li>An unadjusted selection rank equivalent to 50 or above. This may be assessed on the basis of any qualification accepted by the University, which includes (but is not limited to) Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (eg HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, or completed enabling programs; OR</li> <li>One or more years of full-time professional experience (or part-time equivalent) in a relevant field. </li> </ol> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-jshiy7-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1">English language requirements </div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Undergraduate Certificate in Languages requires students to successfully complete 40 units chosen from the course list.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50109?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">The Undergraduate Certificate in Sport and Movement Leadership at the University of Newcastle is designed for individuals seeking a career pathway into a sport-related field. This flexible program allows students to tailor their studies by selecting existing courses from Health and Physical Education, Exercise and Sport Sciences, Business, and Psychology.</div><div aria-hidden="false" class="unset css-1knasfq-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>The Undergraduate Certificate in Sport and Movement Leadership at the University of Newcastle is designed for individuals seeking a career pathway into a sport-related field. This flexible program allows students to tailor their studies by selecting existing courses from Health and Physical Education, Exercise and Sport Sciences, Business, and Psychology.</p></div></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '0 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>To be eligible for admission to the program, applicants must have either:</p> <ol> <li>An unadjusted selection rank equivalent to 50 or above. This may be assessed on the basis of any qualification accepted by the University, which includes (but is not limited to) Australian or overseas senior secondary qualifications (eg HSC), prior tertiary studies, prior TAFE/VET studies, or completed enabling programs; OR</li> <li>One or more years of full-time professional experience (or part-time equivalent) in a relevant field.</li> </ol> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>The Undergraduate Certificate in Sport and Movement Leadership is a 0.5 year program (or part-time equivalent) requiring students to complete 40 units consisting of:</p> <ul><li>20 units of core courses; and</li><li>20 units selected from the course list.</li></ul> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50110?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="css-c314iz-Box--Box-Box-Card--Card-Card-EmptyCard--EmptyCard e90ryr82" elevation="3" id="Description"><div class="css-3chzt3-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardHeader e12hqxty2"><h3 class="css-1ufd5bs-EmptyCard--CardTitle e90ryr81" data-testid="module-header-Description" font-size="1.35rem" font-weight="600">Description </h3></div><div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div aria-hidden="false" class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">Yapug is a free pathway program offered at the University of Newcastle for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people who are wanting to: Gain admission to an undergraduate degree at the University of Newcastle;Develop the academic skills necessary to succeed at university level;Become familiar with the University of Newcastle and… For more content click the Read More button below.</div><div aria-hidden="true" class="closed clamp css-1nicxnb-ReadMore--Body e1ydu1r41" data-testid="read-more-body" style="padding-bottom: 16px; max-height: none; -webkit-line-clamp: unset;"><div class="readmore-content-wrapper"><p>Yapug is a free pathway program offered at the University of Newcastle for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people who are wanting to:</p> <ul><li>Gain admission to an undergraduate degree at the University of Newcastle;</li><li>Develop the academic skills necessary to succeed at university level;</li><li>Become familiar with the University of Newcastle and its environment; and</li><li>Develop different learning methods and skills, including problem-based learning, whilst enjoying a supportive learning environment (culturally, personally and academically).</li></ul> <p>Yapug offers flexible study options. You can choose to study:</p> <ul><li>Full-time over one year (two semesters); or</li><li>Part-time over two years (three or four semesters).</li></ul> <p>Upon successful completion of Yapug you will receive a Certificate of Attainment, will be guaranteed entry to over 70 degrees; and will also be able to use your final grades for competitive admission to all other degrees at the University.</p></div></div><div class="css-v3erwk-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex-ReadMore--Footer e1ydu1r40"><button class="css-1bi3qt-SLinkButton--CallToActionButton erbjvpb0" color="">Read More <div class="css-1jekr9z-ReadMore--SROnly e1ydu1r42">about Description</div></button></div></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '1 years',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-yd08g9-Box--Box-Box-Attribute--AttrContainer ene3w3n3" display=""><div class="css-t643gp-Attribute--AttrBody ene3w3n1" data-testid="AttrBody"><div class="css-19qn38w-Box--Box-Box-Flex--Flex-Flex e8qda2r1"> </div><div class="css-1nx81rv-Attribute--AttributeChildrenWrap ene3w3n0"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>To be eligible for admission applicants must:</p> <ol> <li>be an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person;</li> <li>not have successfully completed an enabling program or tertiary studies at either the University of Newcastle or any other higher education institution (with the exception of the Elite Athletes Pathway Program);</li> <li>be 17 or older prior to submitting an application; and</li> <li>meet any other admission criteria prescribed at the time of application.</li> </ol> <p><strong>Minimum English language proficiency requirements</strong></p> <p>Pathway programs, such as Yapug, require students to have a good level of written and spoken English. It is assumed that you have undertaken some formal study in English prior to commencing.</p> <p>Academic Learning Support and Indigenous Academic Learning Support will be available to help you develop your language skills including:</p> <ul> <li>Academic reading and writing (including essays and reports)</li> <li>Preparing for assignments and exams</li> <li>Academic language (grammar/vocabulary/learning strategies and practices)</li> </ul> </div></div></div></div></div> <div class="css-1bxk47o-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><div class="css-apyj4p-Box--Box-Box-Card--CardBody e12hqxty1"><p>To successfully complete Yapug you need to successfully complete a combined total of 80 units (made up of 8 x 10 unit courses):</p> <ul><li>40 units of core courses;</li><li>40 units of courses chosen from the course list.</li></ul> <p>It is important to consider the undergraduate degree you’d like to study upon the completion of Yapug, as the courses you choose help to prepare you for that area of study. You should explore the list of <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0009/861435/Recommended-Courses.pdf" rel="nofollow">recommended courses</a> to see what is suggested for the programs you are interested in.</p> </div></div>',
    apply_form = 'https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11195?year=2026',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '';
